From bd94bda0887acb368f86c681c0b181642fb6657c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "PM.RAZOR" <hslee1659@naver.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 14:08:40 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/9] Fix crashes and rendering bugs found while porting SSX
 (2012)

- Input: serialize InputSystem entry points; concurrent guest polling
  rebuilt devices_ under other readers and crashed in RefreshDevices.
- Config/achievement/log TOML loading: open files via std::filesystem::path
  so non-ASCII (e.g. Korean) user folders load on Windows.
- D3D12 texture cache: clamp small-mip copies of resolution-scaled
  textures to the destination subresource (odd sizes overran it and removed
  the device with INVALID_CALL); size the 3D-as-2D wrapper by the draw
  resolution scale like xenia-canary.
- D3D12 render target cache: 8_8_8_8 <-> 8_8_8_8_GAMMA ownership transfer
  converted in the wrong direction (inverted vs Xenia).
- New diagnostics (off by default): --d3d12_diagnose_invalid_command_lists
  bisects a command list that fails Close() and logs the first invalid
  command; --log_wait_stats logs per-thread guest wait call sites.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
