Guest code resolves into one slice of large 2D arrays per frame (SSX: a
128x128x256 snow trail atlas), and the texture cache reloaded the whole
array on every change - about 80% of all texture load work in races with
resolution scaling. A global watch now accumulates the range written by the
GPU while the base is outdated, and the D3D12 load only processes those
slices. CPU writes or initial loads still reload everything.
