the previous change never applied. The Xenos 3D tiled address is linear in
whole groups of 8 depth slices (odd and even groups of 4 interleave
differently), so GPU-written ranges map to 8-slice groups, and the load
shader starts at a group boundary with shifted guest/host offsets. The
texture load log now counts the texels actually processed.

